+# Plan: Security Group detail tabs on Juno `TabBar`/`TabBarItem`
+
+**Date:** 2026-10-28 · **Status:** not implemented
+**Base:** `main` @ `8cd09bfa`
+
+## Overview
+
+Issue #1387 asks for the Security Group detail page's "Rules" and "RBAC Policies" tabs to use Juno's `TabBar`/`TabBarItem`. Those components replace the deprecated `TabNavigation`/`TabNavigationItem`. The screenshot in the issue is out of date: it shows the hand-rolled `<button>` tabs that PR #1375 already replaced with `TabNavigation`. So the work left is replacing the deprecated `TabNavigation` with `TabBar`, plus three small additions: a landmark `ariaLabel` on the tab bar, an update to the Copilot review rule that still requires `TabNavigation`, and a patch changeset. Behavior does not change: the tab state stays local, and the look, keyboard handling and `aria-current` semantics stay the same.
+
+## Decisions
+
+- **D1.** Should `.github/copilot-instructions.md:130`, which still names `TabNavigation`, be updated in this change? → **A: yes.** The "Tab navigation" row becomes `TabBar`, `TabBarItem`.
+- **D2.** Should the active tab move into a URL search param? → **A: no.** It stays in local `useState` in `SecurityGroupDetailsView.tsx`. URL sync is proposed as a follow-up.
+- **Small choices (accepted):**
+  - use `TabBar`'s default appearance (`"tabs"`)
+  - add `ariaLabel={t\`Security group sections\`}` and regenerate the catalogs with `check-i18n`
+  - keep the component's public API and existing tests
+  - add a patch changeset
+  - list the other five `TabNavigation` users as one proposed follow-up
+
+## Architecture Analysis
+
+**Current state:**
+
+- `packages/aurora/src/client/routes/_auth/projects/$projectId/network/securitygroups/$securityGroupId/-components/-details/SecurityGroupTabs.tsx` renders the tabs with `TabNavigation` (`className="mt-4"`, `activeItem={activeTab}`, `onActiveItemChange` narrowed through `isTabType`). It has two `TabNavigationItem`s:
+  - `value="rules"`, `label={t\`Rules\`}`
+  - `value="rbac"`, `label={t\`RBAC Policies\`}`, rendered only when `showRBACTab`
+
+  Each item also gets `active={activeTab === "<value>"}`. Exports: `SecurityGroupTabs` and `TabType = "rules" | "rbac"`, re-exported from `-details/index.ts`.
+- `.../$securityGroupId/-components/SecurityGroupDetailsView.tsx` owns the state:
+  - `useState<TabType>("rules")`
+  - `showRBACTab = isOwner && permissions.canViewRBAC`
+  - `currentTab` falls back to `"rules"` when the RBAC tab is hidden
+
+  It renders `<SecurityGroupTabs activeTab={currentTab} onTabChange={setActiveTab} showRBACTab={showRBACTab} />`. This file needs no change.
+- Tests:
+  - `SecurityGroupTabs.test.tsx` already asserts `getByRole("button", { name })`, `aria-current="true"`, that the component follows `activeTab` after a click, `onTabChange("rbac")`, and that the RBAC tab is hidden when `showRBACTab={false}`.
+  - `SecurityGroupDetailsView.test.tsx:176-198` covers the fallback to Rules when the RBAC tab disappears.
+- **Juno at the installed 9.7.1** (`packages/aurora/package.json`; checked in `node_modules/.../build/index.d.ts:86-89` and the `@cloudoperators/juno-ui-components@9.7.1` tag sources):
+  - `TabBar` and `TabBarItem` are exported, and their props are a superset of what we pass (`activeItem`, `ariaLabel`, `className`, `onActiveItemChange: (activeItem: ReactNode) => void`, `appearance`; item: `value`, `label`, `active`, `onClick`, ...).
+  - `TabNavigation` is `withDeprecationWarning(TabNavigationBackwardsCompat)`, i.e. `<TabBar appearance="main" className="juno-tabnavigation ...">`. Mounting it calls `console.warn("TabNavigation is deprecated ...")`.
+  - Both wrap the same `Navigation`/`NavigationItem`: `<nav role="navigation">` → `<li>` → `<button aria-current>`, and `activeItem` is synced through a `useEffect` on `activeItem`. The DOM, the a11y semantics and the activeItem-sync quirk documented in the current code comment are therefore unchanged.
+  - Item styles for `"main"` and `"tabs"` are identical (`tabBarItemStyles`). No CSS targets the `juno-tabbar-*`/`juno-tabnavigation-*` class names, so the default `"tabs"` appearance looks the same as today.
+  - The ui-components skills (`node_modules/@cloudoperators/juno-ui-components/skills/`, consumed since c65b36d0) cover only DataGrid. They have no TabBar guidance.
+- Other `TabNavigation` users (out of scope; see Proposed follow-ups): `client/components/ListToolbar/index.tsx`, `network/routers/-components/RouterDetailsView.tsx`, `storage/-components/Ceph/Buckets/BucketDetailTabs.tsx`, `storage/-components/Ceph/Objects/ObjectBrowserView.tsx`, `compute/images/-components/List.tsx`.
+- `.github/copilot-instructions.md` B.1 table, line 130: `| Tab navigation | \`TabNavigation\`, \`TabNavigationItem\` |`.
+- i18n:
+  - `check-i18n` = `lingui extract --clean && lingui compile --typescript`.
+  - Catalogs are committed in `packages/aurora/src/locales/{en,de}/messages.{po,ts}`.
+  - The German catalog has hundreds of untranslated `msgstr ""` entries, so an untranslated new string is normal.
+
+**Proposed changes:**
+
+- Swap the imports and JSX in `SecurityGroupTabs.tsx` to `TabBar`/`TabBarItem` and add `ariaLabel`. Keep the props, the `TabType` export and the `isTabType` guard.
+- Extend the colocated test with an aria-label check and a no-deprecation-warning guard.
+- Update the Copilot rule row, regenerate the Lingui catalogs, and add a changeset.
+- No server, route, state or data-flow changes, which fits the "Juno components for UI primitives" rule (copilot-instructions B.1).
+
+## Potential Problems & Mitigations
+
+| Risk | Severity | Mitigation |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| Visual difference between the old default `appearance="main"` and the new default `"tabs"` | Low | Verified in the 9.7.1 sources: same item styles, and no CSS keyed on the class names. Confirm visually on the mock (Testing Plan). |
+| `activeItem` stops re-syncing after a click (the quirk the existing comment describes) | Low | Same `Navigation` underneath. The existing test "follows activeTab after a tab has been clicked" and the details-view fallback test guard it. Keep both `activeItem` and per-item `active`. |
+| New Lingui string not extracted, so CI `check-i18n` fails or the catalog diff is stale | Medium | Run `pnpm --filter @cobaltcore-dev/aurora check-i18n` and keep the regenerated `locales/{en,de}/messages.{po,ts}`. |
+| Copilot rule now names `TabBar` while five files still use `TabNavigation` | Low | Accepted under D1. Copilot reviews only changed lines, and the migration of the other scopes is a follow-up. |
+| Prettier reflows the copilot-instructions markdown table (column widths) | Low | Run `pnpm format` (or `prettier --write` on the file) and check with `pnpm format:check`. |
+| The added `ariaLabel` changes the accessible name of the nav landmark | Low (improvement) | Tests query the tab buttons by name, not the nav, so nothing breaks. A new test asserts the label. |
+
+## Prerequisites
+
+- [ ] None. `TabBar`/`TabBarItem` ship in the installed `@cloudoperators/juno-ui-components` 9.7.1, and the local mock already seeds security groups with RBAC policies.
+
+## Implementation Steps
+
+### Step 1: Replace `TabNavigation` with `TabBar` in `SecurityGroupTabs`
+
+**Files to modify/create:**
+
+- `packages/aurora/src/client/routes/_auth/projects/$projectId/network/securitygroups/$securityGroupId/-components/-details/SecurityGroupTabs.tsx` — swap the components and add `ariaLabel`
+
+**What to do:**
+
+1. Change the import to `import { TabBar, TabBarItem } from "@cloudoperators/juno-ui-components"`.
+2. Replace `<TabNavigation ...>` with `<TabBar ...>` and keep `className="mt-4"`, `activeItem={activeTab}` and `onActiveItemChange={(key) => isTabType(key) && onTabChange(key)}`. Add `ariaLabel={t\`Security group sections\`}`. Don't pass `appearance`, so the default `"tabs"` applies.
+3. Replace both `TabNavigationItem`s with `TabBarItem`, keeping `value`, `label` and `active` exactly as they are. Keep the `showRBACTab &&` condition.
+4. Update the comment above the JSX to say "TabBar" instead of "TabNavigation". The behavior it describes still holds. Keep `TabType`, `SecurityGroupTabsProps`, `isTabType` and the export unchanged, so `-details/index.ts` and `SecurityGroupDetailsView.tsx` need no edits.
+
+**Expected outcome:**
+
+- The tabs render from `TabBar`/`TabBarItem`, the browser console shows no "TabNavigation is deprecated" warning on the detail page, and the look and behavior stay the same.
+
+**Verification:**
+
+- `pnpm --filter @cobaltcore-dev/aurora typecheck` passes.
+- `grep -n "TabNavigation" packages/aurora/src/client/routes/_auth/projects/\$projectId/network/securitygroups -r` returns nothing.
+
+---
+
+### Step 2: Extend the colocated tests [CAREFUL]
+
+**Files to modify/create:**
+
+- `.../$securityGroupId/-components/-details/SecurityGroupTabs.test.tsx` — two new cases
+
+**What to do:**
+
+1. Keep all five existing tests unchanged. They must pass as they are, which proves the a11y and DOM behavior is the same.
+2. Add `it("labels the tab navigation", ...)`: render with `activeTab="rules"` and assert `screen.getByRole("navigation", { name: "Security group sections" })` is in the document.
+3. Add `it("does not render deprecated Juno tab components", ...)`: `const warn = vi.spyOn(console, "warn").mockImplementation(() => {})`, render the component, then assert that no call to `warn` received an argument matching `/deprecated/i` (for example `expect(warn.mock.calls.flat().some((a) => /deprecated/i.test(String(a)))).toBe(false)`). Finally call `warn.mockRestore()`. This fails against the old `TabNavigation` code because of Juno's `withDeprecationWarning` `console.warn`.
+
+**Expected outcome:**
+
+- 7 tests pass. The new guard keeps the component from regressing to `TabNavigation`.
+
+**Verification:**
+
+- `pnpm --filter @cobaltcore-dev/aurora test 'src/client/routes/_auth/projects/$projectId/network/securitygroups/$securityGroupId'` is green, including `SecurityGroupDetailsView.test.tsx`.
+
